          <text x="502.6" y="-65" class="t-muted" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">V8 runs it to the end</text>
        </g>

        <g id="node-drain" data-step="drain" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Drain queues — nextTick, then promises" data-detail="When the script returns, Node empties the nextTick queue and V8's promise queue, the same drain that follows every callback. Only then does it call uv_run().">
          <rect x="612.6" y="-98" width="120" height="44" class="c-mask" />
          <rect x="612.6" y="-98" width="120" height="44" class="c-external" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <text x="672.6" y="-79" class="t-primary" font-size="10" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">Drain queues</text>
          <text x="672.6" y="-65" class="t-muted" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">nextTick, promises</text>
        </g>

        <g id="node-start" data-step="start" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="uv_run() starts — timers run once" data-detail="Node calls uv_run() after your main script finishes. Before the while loop, libuv updates its clock and runs any timer that is already due, once. It is a backwards-compatibility leftover from libuv 1.45.0, and it decides the main-script setTimeout vs setImmediate race.">
          <rect x="252.6" y="-14" width="140" height="50" class="c-mask" />
          <rect x="252.6" y="-14" width="140" height="50" class="c-backend" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <text x="322.6" y="4" class="t-primary" font-size="10" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">uv_run() starts</text>
          <text x="322.6" y="17" class="t-muted" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">uv__run_timers(), once</text>
          <text x="322.6" y="29" class="t-backend" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle">before the loop</text>
        </g>

        <g id="node-gate" data-step="gate" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="uv__loop_alive() — any work left?" data-detail="True while an active handle, an active request, a pending callback or a closing handle is left. An open server or an uncleared setInterval keeps it true, and keeps Node running.">
          <rect x="270.6" y="206" width="104" height="68" class="c-mask" />
          <rect x="270.6" y="206" width="104" height="68" class="c-backend" stroke-width="1.5" />
          <g aria-hidden="true" class="semantic-sigil s-backend" transform="translate(276.6 212) scale(0.6875)">
